{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-30T12:44:36.870Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"7b0e58428f53e3aaeaafb372","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.312","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1633"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1633: accept comma-separated --unset field lists with per-field validation"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1633\n\nReported on published 2026.10.28 in a fresh pm init --defaults workspace. pm create/update take --unset <field> once per field. A comma list such as --unset parent,release is refused as one unknown field name, and the refusal neither explains the repeat-the-flag form nor offers a corrected command. Neighbouring list flags on the same commands (--tags a,b) accept commas, so agents carry that spelling over and lose one round-trip per progressive create.\n\nThe report offers two options: (1) accept comma lists, because no field name contains a comma, validating each part and refusing unknown names one by one; (2) keep the single-field contract and add a replay correction. This item adopts option 1 if field-key validation proves commas cannot occur in a field name, and declares the flag as a list in the flag contracts so contracts, help, and recovery agree."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","github","sdk"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-10-30T12:44:36.870Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-30T12:44:36.870Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":90},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Reproduce the reported refusal on current source and the published host; Prove field keys cannot contain commas before splitting; Accept comma lists on create, update and update-many, with every part validated and unknown or empty parts refused individually; Declare --unset as a list in flag contracts, help and docs; Cover CLI and SDK controls, including mixed repeated and comma forms, with a pre-fix negative"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-mpbb"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/reporter","value":"unbraind"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"pm create/update --unset parent,release clears both fields exactly as repeated --unset flags do, and an unknown or empty part is refused by name."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/affected_version","value":"2026.10.28"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/component","value":"cli"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-gh1626","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-10-30T12:44:36.870Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-gknu","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-10-30T12:44:36.870Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-10-30T12:44:36.870Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Duplicate check: semantic search for --unset comma lists (top hits pm-evav, pm-ltbr, pm-hu92i3, pm-cf1u, pm-klqo, pm-kfq5, pm-nc94mk, pm-gknu, all closed), a keyword search for --unset replay corrections, and the 28 open agent-ux items. None of them owns --unset comma handling. The nearest owners are pm-gknu (closed, multi-value filter grammar) and pm-gh1626 (open, sibling same-command correction). Source report: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1633"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"55a57627de97b14a83b62138f4c8a1053fd884de1773cd06d23e4c6c01763466","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"c3f2f081f4af665ca8071c1bc1c5576d44a1f4dbb0a50bce322a04d649f7cd62"}
